-- title:
--   Dimension multiplicativity for Hopf subalgebras of nil Hopf algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $H$ be a commutative ring equipped with a Hopf algebra structure over $k$ which is finite as a $k$-module. Assume that every $x \in H$ with $\varepsilon(x) = 0$ is nilpotent, where $\varepsilon =$ `Coalgebra.counit` is the counit of $H$ over $k$. Let $S$ be a $k$-subalgebra of $H$ which is stable under comultiplication in the following explicit sense: for every $x \in S$, the element $\Delta(x) =$ `Coalgebra.comul` $(x)$ of $H \otimes_k H$ lies in the $k$-span of the set of tensors $a \otimes_k b$ with $a, b \in S$; and assume $S$ is stable under the antipode, i.e. `HopfAlgebra.antipode k x` $\in S$ for all $x \in S$. Then the $k$-dimension of $H$ is the product of the $k$-dimension of $S$ and the $k$-dimension of the quotient of $H$ by the ideal generated by the set $\{x \in H : x \in S \text{ and } \varepsilon(x) = 0\}$, that is, $\dim_k H = \dim_k S \cdot \dim_k (H / S^{+}H)$ with $S^{+}$ the augmentation ideal of $S$.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of orders $|G| = |G''| \cdot |N|$ for a finite commutative group scheme $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$ with infinitesimal (nil augmentation ideal) coordinate ring, the quotient $G'' = \operatorname{Spec} S$ attached to a Hopf subalgebra $S \subseteq H$, and $N = \operatorname{Spec}(H/S^{+}H)$ the kernel of $G \to G''$. It is used in the structure theory of such Hopf algebras, in particular by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_mvPolynomial_quotient_X_pow_of_isNilpotent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_algEquiv_mvPolynomial_quotient_X_pow_of_isNilpotent).
